# aarch64 SNO Deployment — Pitfalls & Fixes

This document catalogs every issue encountered across multiple deployment
attempts on aarch64 SNO OpenShift clusters. **Read it end-to-end before
starting any deployment. Every item here caused real wasted time.**

---

## 1. kcli Downloads the Wrong RHCOS Image (amd64 Instead of aarch64)

**Symptom:** `kcli create cluster` on an aarch64 hypervisor downloads the
x86_64 RHCOS image. The resulting VMs fail to boot or crash immediately.

**Root Cause:** kcli's default RHCOS image URL points to x86_64. It does
not auto-detect the hypervisor architecture.

**Fix:** Patch the kcli plan or explicitly pass the aarch64 RHCOS image URL:

```bash
# Find the correct aarch64 RHCOS URL for your OCP version
RHCOS_URL="https://mirror.openshift.com/pub/openshift-v4/aarch64/dependencies/rhcos/<version>/rhcos-<version>-qemu.aarch64.qcow2.gz"

# Pass it to kcli
kcli create cluster openshift \
  --paramfile sno.yml \
  -P image_url=$RHCOS_URL
```

**Rule:** On aarch64 hypervisors, ALWAYS verify the RHCOS image architecture
before starting cluster creation. Never assume kcli picks the right one.

