## 5. RHBK v26: Admin Username Is "temp-admin", Not "admin"

**Symptom:** `curl` to Keycloak master realm token endpoint returns
`{"error":"invalid_grant","error_description":"Invalid user credentials"}`
when using username `admin`.

**Root Cause:** RHBK operator sets the initial admin username to
`temp-admin` (not `admin`) in the `keycloak-initial-admin` secret.

**Fix:** Always read both username AND password from the secret:

```bash
ADMIN_USER=$(oc get secret keycloak-initial-admin -n keycloak \
  -o jsonpath='{.data.username}' | base64 -d)
ADMIN_PASS=$(oc get secret keycloak-initial-admin -n keycloak \
  -o jsonpath='{.data.password}' | base64 -d)
```

**Rule:** Never hardcode `admin` as the Keycloak admin username. Always
read it from the secret.

