## 9. Hypervisor `/etc/hosts` Must Include ALL Route Hostnames

**Symptom:** Scripts running on the hypervisor timeout with "Timeout waiting
for Keycloak admin API" or `curl` returns connection refused for routes.

**Root Cause:** The hypervisor can reach the SNO cluster's VIP but has no
DNS for `*.apps.sno.karmalabs.corp` routes. Scripts use route hostnames
that don't resolve.

**Fix:** Add ALL route hostnames to the hypervisor's `/etc/hosts`:

```
192.168.122.115 api.sno.karmalabs.corp \
  console-openshift-console.apps.sno.karmalabs.corp \
  oauth-openshift.apps.sno.karmalabs.corp \
  default-route-openshift-image-registry.apps.sno.karmalabs.corp \
  keycloak-keycloak.apps.sno.karmalabs.corp \
  cost-onprem-gateway-cost-onprem.apps.sno.karmalabs.corp
```

**Rule:** After creating any new route, immediately add it to the
hypervisor's `/etc/hosts`.

